# UniGetUI's configuration folder is linked whole, and UniGetUI keeps adding runtime state to it (tokens, history,
# window and UI state, what it upgraded on this machine). Only the settings allowed here are shared; anything new
# stays on its machine until it gets a line. `git status --ignored Config/UniGetUI` lists what isn't shared.
Config/UniGetUI/*
!Config/UniGetUI/AlwaysElevate.json
!Config/UniGetUI/AutomaticallyUpdatePackages
!Config/UniGetUI/AutoUpdatedPackages.json
!Config/UniGetUI/CollapseNavMenuOnWideScreen
!Config/UniGetUI/DisableClassicMode
!Config/UniGetUI/DisabledManagers.json
!Config/UniGetUI/DisableInstantSearch.json
!Config/UniGetUI/DoCacheAdminRights
!Config/UniGetUI/EnableScoopCleanup
!Config/UniGetUI/EnableUniGetUIBeta
!Config/UniGetUI/HideToggleFilters.json
!Config/UniGetUI/IgnoredPackageUpdates.json
!Config/UniGetUI/MaintenanceSchedules
!Config/UniGetUI/PackageListViewMode.json
!Config/UniGetUI/PreferredTheme
# One-time flags, kept so a new machine skips the telemetry banner and the import of old WingetUI settings
!Config/UniGetUI/ShownTelemetryBanner
!Config/UniGetUI/TransferredOldSettings
!Config/UniGetUI/TransferredOldSettingsv2
